  "contract": [
    "Destroy current workspace then free the reloaded workspace owner. Do not clear that owner.",
    "Reload the processing owner before each record dispatch at6c,70,84 and each release-clear cell atb0,bc,cc,d8. Free the final live context and return0 without clearing its owner.",
    "Dispatch reads record type and invokes the ordinary C provider corresponding to the stock seven-entry table. Types0,1,2,6 supported;3,4,5 are stock null entries and out-of-range indices are outside the defined contract.",
    "Reuse canonical C workspace/record/nullable/cell providers. The newly mapped6629e helper has release-then-clear semantics; no duplicate provider body added."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "All138 native entry instruction bytes execute. Direct free is modeled with snapshots and caller-scratch clobbers; actual-heap integration executes the C initializer/allocator and every teardown descendant without stock-code fallback.",
    "Fixtures vary all64 supported record type triples, field masks, allocation order and unrelated live allocations. Live owner mutations test re-reads and clear-after-release timing.",
    "Initial null workspace access8, null record/type read0, null cell read0 and null processing context access6c are emulator access-shape checks, not physical MCU fault claims.",
    "Saved integer/FP registers, SP, interrupt masks, FPSCR and caller guards checked. Caller scratch, APSR and private stack frames excluded. The stock transient ROM-table copy has no externally visible effect in the supported immutable-table contract.",
    "Typed context/workspace setup is a fixture rather than recovered initialization. Future processing initialization must use the two canonical owner cells. No initialization, concurrency, physical memory, final executable placement/startup or boot claim. Relocatable composition is not bootable firmware."
  ],
